  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Another cold night in store for central PA.\n\nHigh pressure will slide east overnight, with winds shifting \naround to the SW across west central PA. This should make frost \nless likely tonight in the places that were coldest this \nmorning. However, frost will be possible to the east where winds\nwill be calm, closer to the center of the high. A frost advisory\nfor portions of the east tonight.\n\n-------------------------------------------------------------\n \nKEY MESSAGE 2: Extended stretch of dry and seasonal Fall \nweather this week, followed by a chance of rain on Sunday\ninto Monday.\n\nHigh confidence in a prolonged stretch of dry and seasonable \nFall wx this week with cool nights and refreshing afternoons \nwith low humidity. This will give the area a much needed chance \nto dry out from the wet summer and early fall so far.\n\nThe next chance of rain is on Sunday, as moisture moves up from\nthe Gulf Coast states. However, there is still ample uncertainty\nregarding how much of that moisture makes it into our region.",
